  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Romans",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 13,
    "summary": "Paul counsels, Be subject unto God’s ministers; keep the commandments; love one another; righteousness leads to salvation.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Let every soul be subject unto the higher powers. For there is no power but of God: the powers that be are ordained of God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "GR be submissive, render obedience. D&C 58:22 (21–22). TG Citizenship; Governments."
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "GR authorities."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "John 19:11 (10–12)."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "JST Rom. 13:1 … in the church but of God …"
          },
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "TG Governments."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whosoever therefore resisteth the power, resisteth the ordinance of God: and they that resist shall receive to themselves damnation.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "TG Rebellion."
          },
          {
            "start": 122,
            "end": 131,
            "text": "TG Damnation."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For rulers are not a terror to good works, but to the evil. Wilt thou then not be afraid of the power? do that which is good, and thou shalt have praise of the same:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 101,
            "text": "GR authority."
          },
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 124,
            "text": "TG Retribution."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For he is the minister of God to thee for good. But if thou do that which is evil, be afraid; for he beareth not the sword in vain: for he is the minister of God, a revenger to execute wrath upon him that doeth evil.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "GR a servant."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 177,
            "end": 184
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore ye must needs be subject, not only for wrath, but also for conscience sake.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG Conscience."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For for this cause pay ye tribute also: for they are God’s ministers, attending continually upon this very thing.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "JST Rom. 13:6–7 (Appendix)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Render therefore to all their dues: tribute to whom tribute is due; custom to whom custom; fear to whom fear; honour to whom honour.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 116,
            "text": "D&C 134:6. TG Honor."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Owe no man any thing, but to love one another: for he that loveth another hath fulfilled the law.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "TG Debt."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "TG Love."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For this, Thou shalt not commit adultery, Thou shalt not kill, Thou shalt not steal, Thou shalt not bear false witness, Thou shalt not covet; and if there be any other commandment, it is briefly comprehended in this saying, namely, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Adulterer."
          },
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 83,
            "text": "TG Stealing."
          },
          {
            "start": 135,
            "end": 140,
            "text": "TG Covet."
          },
          {
            "start": 252,
            "end": 261,
            "text": "TG Neighbor."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 149,
            "end": 157
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Love worketh no ill to his neighbour: therefore love is the fulfilling of the law.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "Moro. 7:47 (1, 44–47). TG Motivations."
          },
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "Matt. 22:40 (36–40); Gal. 5:14 (13–14)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And that, knowing the time, that now it is high time to awake out of sleep: for now is our salvation nearer than when we believed.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Time."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "TG Apathy; Sleep."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 86
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The night is far spent, the day is at hand: let us therefore cast off the works of darkness, and let us put on the armour of light.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "John 9:4; Alma 34:31 (31–34)."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "2 Cor. 5:17; 1 Thes. 5:4. TG Darkness, Spiritual."
          },
          {
            "start": 115,
            "end": 121,
            "text": "Isa. 59:17 (16–17); 2 Cor. 6:7; Eph. 6:11 (10–24); 1 Thes. 5:8; D&C 27:15 (15–18)."
          },
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 130,
            "text": "TG Children of Light; Light [noun]."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let us walk honestly, as in the day; not in rioting and drunkenness, not in chambering and wantonness, not in strife and envying.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "GR with propriety, decently, gracefully. TG Honesty."
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Rioting and Reveling."
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "TG Drunkenness."
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "GR lewdness, whoredoms."
          },
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 128,
            "text": "TG Envy."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But put ye on the Lord Jesus Christ, and make not provision for the flesh, to fulfil the lusts thereof.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "Gal. 3:27 (24–29)."
          },
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "TG Lust."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 84
          },
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 103
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
